## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates offline-first architecture design, conflict resolution strategies, and API robustness for clients with unreliable connectivity.

## Key Concepts
- Client-side caching with immediate response
- Version-based conflict resolution using sync tokens
- Idempotent operations for safe retries
- Batch synchronization for network efficiency
- Comprehensive testing under simulated outage conditions

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for offline sync workflow
const cache = new UserScoreCache();
const syncQueue = new OfflineQueue();

function computeCCAScore(userId, data) {
  const score = calculateScore(data);
  const token = cache.update(userId, score);
  syncQueue.enqueue({userId, score, token, timestamp: Date.now()});
  return score;
}

function syncToServer() {
  if (navigator.onLine) {
    const batch = syncQueue.getBatch();
    return fetch('/cca_score/sync', {
      method: 'POST',
      body: JSON.stringify(batch)
    }).then(response => {
      if (response.ok) syncQueue.confirmBatch();
    });
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle concurrent client modifications?
- What fallback strategies would you implement for extended outages?
- How would you optimize sync payload size for low-bandwidth connections?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates your ability to design a privacy-preserving ABAC layer that controls access to encrypted CCA score shares without revealing plaintext data. It tests understanding of dynamic admin access, revocation mechanisms, auditability, and system design at scale.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC attributes: tenant_id, region, role, expiry
- Token-based access without decryption
- Immutable audit logs with tamper-evident provenance
- Key management with per-tenant keys
- Revocation and expiry propagation

## Code Example
```javascript
function evaluatePolicy(attrs, action) {
  const now = Date.now();

  if (attrs.expiry < now) return { allowed: false, reason: 'expired' };
  if (!attrs.tenant_id || !attrs.region) return { allowed: false, reason: 'missing attributes' };

  const policy = getPolicy(attrs.policy_id);
  if (!policy) return { allowed: false, reason: 'policy not found' };

  const regionMatch = policy.regions.includes(attrs.region);
  const roleMatch = policy.roles.includes(attrs.role);

  return { allowed: regionMatch && roleMatch, reason: regionMatch && roleMatch ? 'ok' : 'attribute mismatch' };
}

function revokeAccess(policyId, reason) {
  const policy = getPolicy(policyId);
  policy.revoked = true;
  policy.revocationReason = reason;
  publishRevocationEvent(policyId);
}
```

